module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.EpiLocallySurjective
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PushforwardRightExact
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.Quasicoherent.BigSiteColimits.AffinePresentation
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Descent.FaithfullyFlatModules

/-!
# Generation by global sections, and the descent of images

The two module-theoretic conditions a presenting cover of a ringed site asks for on the slice
site at one of its members — that a quasi-coherent module there is a quotient of a coproduct of
copies of the structure sheaf, and that the relations between those generators are again such a
quotient — are reduced here to a single condition on *sections*: that every section of the
module is, after restriction along the arrows of some covering sieve, an `R`-combination of
restrictions of sections over the terminal object of the slice site.  Over the slice site at an
affine object of a big site of schemes the terminal object is the affine object itself, so the
condition reads: a quasi-coherent module is locally generated by its sections over the affine
base.

The reduction is the whole of the sheaf-theoretic bookkeeping.  Generation by a family of
sections is an epimorphism out of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf; an epimorphism
of sheaves of modules is a locally surjective morphism; and the image of the morphism induced by
a family of sections contains the span of that family, because each summand of the coproduct
hits its own section and an image is a submodule.  No cohomology vanishing and no sheafification
computation enter.

The ring-theoretic half of the same circle of ideas is recorded in the second half of the file:
a descent datum whose descended module consists of values of a map makes that map's values span
after a flat base change, the descended module is the equalizer of the two comparisons on a
double overlap, and membership in the image of a map descends along a faithfully flat base
change presented by isomorphisms.  These are the statements a cover of an affine object by an
affine object supplies, through `Module.Descent`; the first feeds the span condition and the
last feeds surjectivity on global sections, which is the one open hypothesis of
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation.of_isColimit_cokernelCofork_of_surjective_val_app`.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.globalSectionSpan`: the submodule of sections over an object spanned by the
  restrictions of the sections over a terminal object.
* `SheafOfModules.IsLocallySpannedBySections`: every section is, after restriction along the
  arrows of some covering sieve, in that span.
* `SheafOfModules.HasLocallySpannedRelations`: the same condition for the kernel of every
  covering of the universe lift of the module by a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf.
* `SheafOfModules.JointlyDetectsRange`: a family of arrows to a terminal object along which
  membership in the image of a morphism descends.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` and
  `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections`: the generators half of a
  global presentation from the span condition.
* `SheafOfModules.hasGeneratedRelations_of_isLocallySpannedBySections`: the relations half.
* `SheafOfModules.isLocallySpannedBySections_of_forall_exists_cover`: the span condition may be
  tested on a covering family of each object.
* `SheafOfModules.surjective_val_app_of_jointlyDetectsRange`: a locally surjective morphism is
  surjective on sections over a terminal object as soon as every covering sieve of that object
  contains a family which jointly detects images.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.presentingCoverOfAffineOfIsLocallySpannedBySections`: the
  resulting form of the two module-theoretic fields of a presenting cover for the affine objects
  of a category fibred in groupoids over a big fppf category of schemes.
* `Module.Descent.span_range_eq_top_of_descended_le`,
  `Module.Descent.mem_descended_iff_of_comparison`,
  `Module.Descent.mem_range_of_mem_range_of_baseChangeEquiv` and
  `Module.Descent.surjective_of_surjective_of_baseChangeEquiv`: the ring-level statements listed
  above.

## Implementation notes

Memberships are stated for `PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ`, the restriction map bundled as a
semilinear map, rather than for `PresheafOfModules.map`: the latter lands in the restriction of
scalars of the target, whose additive structure is only definitionally that of the target, so a
membership written with it is not closed by the submodule lemmas.
`SheafOfModules.globalSectionSpan_eq_span_range` records that the span is the span of the range
of one semilinear map, which is the shape the ring-level statements produce.

The two halves of the file meet at the ring structure on the sections of the structure sheaf. A
`SheafOfModules.{m} R` has `R : Sheaf J RingCat`, so its sections carry a ring and nothing more,
while descent of modules needs a commutative ring and an algebra structure on the sections over
the cover.  On a big site of schemes those are present — the structure sheaf is the global
functions, a commutative ring — but only through `CategoryTheory.forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat`,
which instance search does not unfold.  The span and detection conditions of the first half are
therefore stated with no commutativity, and the ring-level statements of the second half with
plain types, so that the identification is made once, where the structure sheaf is in hand,
rather than carried through every statement.

What is *not* proved here is the comparison isomorphism that the ring-level statements take as
data: that for a quasi-coherent module `N` on the slice site at an affine object with ring `A`,
and an object of the slice with affine total space and ring `B`, the sections of `N` there are
the base change along `A → B` of the sections over the affine object.  Quasi-coherence on a site
is the existence of a global presentation locally
(`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite`, Stacks 03DL(6)), and a global presentation is a
cokernel of a map between coproducts *of sheaves*; reading sections off it over an affine object
requires both that the sections of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf are the direct
sum of the sections and that sections are exact on the presenting cokernel, the latter being the
vanishing of the first cohomology of a quasi-coherent module on an affine (Stacks 03DW).  The
double-overlap comparison which would define the coaction of a descent datum on the sections
over the cover is the same statement for the projection of that overlap, so a descent datum
cannot be extracted from quasi-coherence alone.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06WN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06WN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w u v r m t

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{r}}

/-- The submodule of the sections of `N` over `W` spanned by the restrictions of the sections
over a terminal object `T`, that is, by the global sections of `N`. -/
noncomputable def globalSectionSpan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    (W : C) : Submodule (R.obj.obj (op W)) (N.val.obj (op W)) :=
  Submodule.span _ (Set.range fun x : N.val.obj (op T) => N.val.overTerminal hT x (op W))

/-- `SheafOfModules.globalSectionSpan` is the span of the range of the restriction map from the
terminal object, which is the form the ring-theoretic descent statements take. -/
lemma globalSectionSpan_eq_span_range {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    (W : C) :
    N.globalSectionSpan hT W =
      Submodule.span (R.obj.obj (op W)) (Set.range (N.val.restrictₛₗ (hT.from W).op)) := rfl

/-- The restriction to `W` of a section of `N` over the terminal object lies in the span of the
global sections over `W`. -/
lemma overTerminal_mem_globalSectionSpan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    (W : C) (x : N.val.obj (op T)) :
    N.val.overTerminal hT x (op W) ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- Restriction carries the span of the global sections into the span of the global sections. -/
lemma restrict_mem_globalSectionSpan {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    {V W : C} (g : W ⟶ V) {n : N.val.obj (op V)} (hn : n ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT V) :
    N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op n ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W := by
  induction hn using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem n hn =>
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hn
    rw [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, N.val.overTerminal_map hT x g.op]
    exact N.overTerminal_mem_globalSectionSpan hT W x
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add n n' _ _ h h' => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem h h'
  | smul a n _ h => rw [map_smulₛₗ]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site with a terminal object `T` is *locally spanned by its global
sections* when every section is, after restriction along the arrows of some covering sieve, an
`R`-combination of restrictions of sections over `T`. -/
def IsLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : C) (n : N.val.obj (op V)), ∃ S : Sieve V, S ∈ J V ∧
    ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (g : W ⟶ V), S g → N.val.restrictₛₗ g.op n ∈ N.globalSectionSpan hT W

/-- The span of a family of global sections at any object is contained in the image of the
induced morphism out of the coproduct of copies of the universe lift of the structure sheaf:
each summand hits the corresponding section, and an image is a submodule. -/
lemma globalSectionSpan_le_range_sigmaDesc {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R} {I : Type (max t r)}
    [HasCoproduct fun _ : I => uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)]
    (s : I → N.val.obj (op T)) (W : C) :
    Submodule.span (R.obj.obj (op W))
        (Set.range fun i => N.val.overTerminal hT (s i) (op W)) ≤
      LinearMap.range
        ((Sigma.desc fun i => fromUliftUnit.{u, v, r, t} hT (s i)).val.app (op W)).hom := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro y ⟨i, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨(Sigma.ι (fun _ : I => uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)) i).val.app
    (op W) (uliftUnitGen.{u, v, r, t} R (op W)), ?_⟩
  have h := congrArg
    (fun φ : uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R) ⟶ N =>
      φ.val.app (op W) (uliftUnitGen.{u, v, r, t} R (op W)))
    (Sigma.ι_comp_desc (fun j => fromUliftUnit.{u, v, r, t} hT (s j)) i)
  refine h.trans ?_
  rw [fromUliftUnit_val_app]
  exact ModuleCat.uliftSelfHom_uliftSelfGen.{r, t} _ _

/-- **A sheaf of modules locally spanned by its global sections is generated by copies of the
structure sheaf.**  The morphism out of the coproduct indexed by *all* sections over the
terminal object is locally surjective, because a section lands in the span of the global
sections after restriction along a covering sieve, and that span lies in its image. -/
theorem isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {N : SheafOfModules.{max t r} R}
    [HasCoproduct fun _ : N.val.obj (op T) => uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)]
    (h : N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT) :
    IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, t} (unit R)) N := by
  refine isGeneratedBy_of_epi_sigmaDesc.{u, v, r, t} hT (fun x => x) ?_
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.EpiMono.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _ ⟨fun {W} n => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hspan⟩ := h W n
  refine J.superset_covering (fun W' g hg => ?_) hS
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := globalSectionSpan_le_range_sigmaDesc.{u, v, r, t} hT (fun x => x) W'
    (hspan g hg)
  exact ⟨y, hy⟩

/-- Being locally spanned by global sections may be tested on a covering family of each object:
the condition at a member of the family propagates to the whole sieve it generates, because
restriction carries the span of the global sections into the span of the global sections. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_of_forall_exists_cover {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (N : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    (h : ∀ V : C, ∃ (I : Type w) (W : I → C) (g : ∀ i, W i ⟶ V),
      Sieve.ofArrows W g ∈ J V ∧ ∀ i, N.globalSectionSpan hT (W i) = ⊤) :
    N.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  intro V n
  obtain ⟨I, W, g, hcov, htop⟩ := h V
  refine ⟨Sieve.ofArrows W g, hcov, fun {W'} a ha => ?_⟩
  rw [Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff] at ha
  obtain ⟨i, c, rfl⟩ := ha
  have key : N.val.restrictₛₗ (c ≫ g i).op n =
      N.val.restrictₛₗ c.op (N.val.restrictₛₗ (g i).op n) := by
    simp only [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, op_comp]
    exact N.val.map_comp_apply _ _ n
  rw [key]
  exact N.restrict_mem_globalSectionSpan hT c
    (Submodule.eq_top_iff'.1 (htop i) (N.val.restrictₛₗ (g i).op n))

/-- Being locally spanned by global sections passes to the universe lift in which global
presentations are taken: the lift of a section over the terminal object is a section over the
terminal object of the lift, and lifting is additive and compatible with the scalars. -/
lemma up_mem_globalSectionSpan_uliftForPresentation {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (W : C) {x : M.val.obj (op W)}
    (hx : x ∈ M.globalSectionSpan hT W) :
    (ULift.up x : ULift.{max u v r} (M.val.obj (op W))) ∈
      (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M).globalSectionSpan hT W := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨ULift.up z, rfl⟩
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add y y' _ _ hy hy' => exact add_mem hy hy'
  | smul a y _ hy => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hy

/-- The universe lift of a sheaf of modules locally spanned by its global sections is again
locally spanned by its global sections. -/
theorem isLocallySpannedBySections_uliftForPresentation {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (h : M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT) :
    (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M).IsLocallySpannedBySections hT := by
  intro V n
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hspan⟩ := h V n.down
  exact ⟨S, hS, fun {W} g hg => up_mem_globalSectionSpan_uliftForPresentation hT M W (hspan g hg)⟩

/-- `SheafOfModules.isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections` for the universe in which global
presentations are taken, with the sheafification instances it needs supplied. -/
private theorem isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpanned_max {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {Z : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R} (h : Z.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT) :
    IsGeneratedBy (uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R)) Z := by
  have h1 : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m, v, u} J
  have h2 : J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r m} :=
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r m,
      u, v} J
  exact isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpannedBySections.{u, v, r, max u v m} hT h

/-- **The generators half of a global presentation, from generation by global sections.**  A
sheaf of modules locally spanned by its sections over a terminal object of the site satisfies
`SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByUnit`. -/
theorem isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    {M : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (h : M.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT) :
    M.IsGeneratedByUnit := by
  exact isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpanned_max.{u, v, r, m} hT
    (isLocallySpannedBySections_uliftForPresentation hT h)

/-- The relations half of a global presentation in section-level form: the kernel of every
covering of the universe lift of `M` by a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf is locally
spanned by its global sections.  The quantification matches that of
`SheafOfModules.HasGeneratedRelations`, so the kernel is presented as a limit fork and no
sheafification instance is needed to state the condition. -/
def HasLocallySpannedRelations {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T) (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ (I : Type (max u v r m)) (P : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : I, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v m} (unit R) ⟶ P),
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι) →
    ∀ b : P ⟶ uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, m, max u v r} M, Epi b →
    ∀ (Z : SheafOfModules.{max u v r m} R) (k : Z ⟶ P) (hk : k ≫ b = 0),
      IsLimit (KernelFork.ofι k hk) → Z.IsLocallySpannedBySections hT

/-- **The relations half of a global presentation, from generation by global sections.**  If the
kernel of every covering of the universe lift of `M` by a coproduct of copies of the structure
sheaf is locally spanned by its global sections, then `M` satisfies
`SheafOfModules.HasGeneratedRelations`. -/
theorem hasGeneratedRelations_of_isLocallySpannedBySections {T : C} (hT : IsTerminal T)
    (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) (h : M.HasLocallySpannedRelations hT) :
    M.HasGeneratedRelations := by
  intro I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ
  exact isGeneratedBy_of_isLocallySpanned_max.{u, v, r, m} hT (h I P ι hP b hb Z k hk hZ)

/-- A family of arrows to a terminal object `T` *jointly detects images* of `b` when a section
of the target over `T` whose restriction along every member of the family is a value of `b` is
itself a value of `b`.  This is the descent property that makes a locally surjective morphism
surjective on global sections. -/
def JointlyDetectsRange {P N : SheafOfModules.{m} R} (b : P ⟶ N) {T : C} {I : Type w}
    {V : I → C} (g : ∀ i, V i ⟶ T) : Prop :=
  ∀ n : N.val.obj (op T),
    (∀ i, N.val.restrictₛₗ (g i).op n ∈ LinearMap.range (b.val.app (op (V i))).hom) →
      n ∈ LinearMap.range (b.val.app (op T)).hom

/-- **A locally surjective morphism is surjective on sections over a terminal object**, provided
every covering sieve of that object contains a family which jointly detects images.  No
cohomology vanishing is used: local surjectivity produces one covering sieve, that of the
sections of the target which lift, and the detection hypothesis is applied to it.  A different
covering sieve is allowed for each section. -/
theorem surjective_val_app_of_jointlyDetectsRange {T : C} {P N : SheafOfModules.{m} R}
    (b : P ⟶ N)
    (hb : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map b.val))
    (hdet : ∀ S : Sieve T, S ∈ J T → ∃ (I : Type w) (V : I → C) (g : ∀ i, V i ⟶ T),
      (∀ i, S (g i)) ∧ JointlyDetectsRange.{w} b g) :
    Function.Surjective (b.val.app (op T)) := by
  intro n
  have := hb
  obtain ⟨I, V, g, hgS, hjd⟩ := hdet _
    (Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map b.val) (U := op T) n)
  exact hjd n fun i => by obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hgS i; exact ⟨y, hy⟩

end SheafOfModules

namespace Module.Descent

open TensorProduct

variable (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- **A descent datum whose descended module is already a set of values spans.**  If every
element of the module descended from a descent datum on `N` is a value of `f : M →ₗ[A] N` and
`B` is flat over `A`, then `N` is spanned over `B` by the values of `f`.

This is the ring-level form of the statement that a quasi-coherent module on a flat cover of an
affine base is generated by the sections it receives from the base: `f` is the restriction map
and the descended module is the submodule of sections that descend. -/
theorem span_range_eq_top_of_descended_le {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N]
    [IsScalarTower A B N] [Module.Flat A B] (d : Datum A B N) {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] (f : M →ₗ[A] N) (hd : ∀ n ∈ d.descended, n ∈ LinearMap.range f) :
    Submodule.span B (Set.range f) = ⊤ :=
  top_le_iff.1 (d.span_descended_eq_top ▸ Submodule.span_mono fun x hx => hd x hx)

/-- **The descended module is the equalizer of the two comparisons on the double overlap.**  Let
`p` and `q` be two maps out of `N` which an injection `e` out of `B ⊗[A] N` identifies with the
coaction and with `n ↦ 1 ⊗ₜ n`.  Then the module descended from the datum is exactly the set on
which `p` and `q` agree.

For a sheaf of modules on a cover `V → U` the two maps are the restrictions to `V ×_U V`, `e` is
the comparison identifying the sections over `V ×_U V` with a base change of the sections over
`V`, and the sheaf condition identifies the set where they agree with the sections over `U`; so
this lemma is what turns the sheaf axiom into the hypothesis of
`Module.Descent.span_range_eq_top_of_descended_le`. -/
theorem mem_descended_iff_of_comparison {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N]
    [IsScalarTower A B N] {N₂ : Type*} [AddCommGroup N₂] [Module A N₂] (d : Datum A B N)
    (e : B ⊗[A] N →ₗ[A] N₂) (he : Function.Injective e) (p q : N →ₗ[A] N₂)
    (hp : ∀ n, p n = e (d.coaction n)) (hq : ∀ n, q n = e ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] n)) {n : N} :
    n ∈ d.descended ↔ p n = q n := by
  rw [Datum.mem_descended_iff, hp, hq]
  exact ⟨fun h => congrArg e h, fun h => he h⟩

variable [Module.FaithfullyFlat A B]
variable {M M' MB M'B : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [AddCommGroup M'] [Module A M']
variable [AddCommGroup MB] [Module B MB] [AddCommGroup M'B] [Module B M'B]

/-- **Membership in the image descends along a faithfully flat base change presented by
isomorphisms.**  Let `f : M →ₗ[A] M'` and `fB : MB →ₗ[B] M'B` be identified by isomorphisms
`B ⊗[A] M ≃ₗ[B] MB` and `B ⊗[A] M' ≃ₗ[B] M'B`, as happens for a map of quasi-coherent modules
restricted to a flat cover.  Then an element of `M'` whose image in `M'B` is a value of `fB` is
already a value of `f`.

Only `Module.Descent.mem_range_of_one_tmul_mem_range` carries content here; the two
isomorphisms serve to transport the hypothesis to the base change of `f`. -/
theorem mem_range_of_mem_range_of_baseChangeEquiv (f : M →ₗ[A] M') (fB : MB →ₗ[B] M'B)
    (eM : B ⊗[A] M ≃ₗ[B] MB) (eM' : B ⊗[A] M' ≃ₗ[B] M'B)
    (hsq : ∀ x : B ⊗[A] M, fB (eM x) = eM' (LinearMap.lTensor B f x))
    {m' : M'} (hm : eM' ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] m') ∈ LinearMap.range fB) :
    m' ∈ LinearMap.range f := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hm
  refine mem_range_of_one_tmul_mem_range A B f ⟨eM.symm y, eM'.injective ?_⟩
  rw [← hsq, eM.apply_symm_apply, hy]

/-- **Surjectivity descends along a faithfully flat base change presented by isomorphisms.**
The elementwise form of `Module.Descent.mem_range_of_mem_range_of_baseChangeEquiv`: if `fB` is
surjective then so is `f`. -/
theorem surjective_of_surjective_of_baseChangeEquiv (f : M →ₗ[A] M') (fB : MB →ₗ[B] M'B)
    (eM : B ⊗[A] M ≃ₗ[B] MB) (eM' : B ⊗[A] M' ≃ₗ[B] M'B)
    (hsq : ∀ x : B ⊗[A] M, fB (eM x) = eM' (LinearMap.lTensor B f x))
    (hfB : Function.Surjective fB) : Function.Surjective f :=
  fun _ => mem_range_of_mem_range_of_baseChangeEquiv A B f fB eM eM' hsq (hfB _)

end Module.Descent

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  {𝒳 : Type v} [Category.{w} 𝒳] (p : 𝒳 ⥤ BigFppfOver B S hS)

/-- **Quasi-coherent modules are globally presented on the slice site at an affine object**,
given that on those slice sites a quasi-coherent module and the relations between its generators
are each spanned, locally, by their sections over the affine object itself.  This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isGeneratedByUnit` with its two
categorical hypotheses replaced by the section-level span conditions of this file; the terminal
object of the slice site at `x` is `CategoryTheory.Over.mk (𝟙 x)`. -/
theorem hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isLocallySpannedBySections (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids)
    (hgen : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (N : SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i))),
      N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
        N.IsLocallySpannedBySections (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := affineObj B S hS p i)) ∧
          N.HasLocallySpannedRelations (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := affineObj B S hS p i)))
    (M : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf))
    (hM : M.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (i : AffineObjects B S hS p) :
    (M.over (affineObj B S hS p i)).HasGlobalPresentation :=
  hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isGeneratedByUnit B S hS p hp
    (fun j N hN =>
      ⟨SheafOfModules.isGeneratedByUnit_of_isLocallySpannedBySections _ (hgen j N hN).1,
        SheafOfModules.hasGeneratedRelations_of_isLocallySpannedBySections _ _ (hgen j N hN).2⟩)
    M hM i

/-- **The affine objects as a presenting cover, from generation by sections over the affine
objects.**  This is `AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.presentingCoverOfAffine` with its
global-presentation field replaced by the two section-level span conditions of this file. -/
def presentingCoverOfAffineOfIsLocallySpannedBySections (hp : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) (K : Type u)
    [Category.{u} K]
    (hgen : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (N : SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i))),
      N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite →
        N.IsLocallySpannedBySections (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := affineObj B S hS p i)) ∧
          N.HasLocallySpannedRelations (Over.mkIdTerminal (X := affineObj B S hS p i)))
    (hcolim : ∀ (i : AffineObjects B S hS p)
      (D : K ⥤ SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf).over (affineObj B S hS p i)))
      (c : Cocone D), IsColimit c → (∀ k, (D.obj k).HasGlobalPresentation) →
        c.pt.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.PresentingCover
      (ringStructureSheafCore B S hS p hp .fppf) K :=
  presentingCoverOfAffine B S hS p hp K
    (fun M hM i =>
      hasGlobalPresentation_over_of_isLocallySpannedBySections B S hS p hp hgen M hM i)
    hcolim

end AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite

